{ "Follow in-game", "跟随游戏内设置" },
{ "Follows per-pixel agreement between the two paths instead of handing\nover every type-1 pixel equally. Whether RR damaged a pixel is a\nper-pixel fact, so one flat weight is the wrong instrument for it.\nWhere the two agree structurally the choice is moot and RR wins on\nstability; where they diverge, RR removed something the floor kept,\nwhich is the case the handover exists for. 0 is off.", "按两条路径逐像素的一致程度来决定，而不是把每个 type-1 像素\n都同等地 handover。RR 是否损坏了某个像素是逐像素的事实，\n所以用一个统一权重来处理并不合适。\n两者在结构上一致的地方，选哪个都无所谓，RR 胜在稳定；\n两者出现分歧的地方，说明 RR 去掉了 floor 保留下来的东西，\n这正是 handover 存在的意义。0 为关闭。" },
{ "For NR pick mochizuki or lmxxf, or set [DlssNr] HostComputeBackend=HIP (no DLSS-FG),\nthen restart the game.", "要用 NR，请选择 mochizuki 或 lmxxf，或设置 [DlssNr] HostComputeBackend=HIP\n（无 DLSS-FG），然后重启游戏。" },
{ "For fine tuning the depth cutoff\nShows UI and depth cutoff areas\nAdjust depth cutoff so that only stuff like your gun and hands are marked", "用于微调深度裁切\n显示 UI 和深度裁切区域\n调整深度裁切，让只有你的枪和手之类的东西被标记" },
{ "For games that change their render resolution as they run. Auto: once it drops\nbelow the game's colour buffer, one network, built for the largest resolution\nseen, serves every frame, which moves inside it; the network then costs that\nlargest resolution's time. Exact: the network is rebuilt for each resolution, a\nsecond or two without NR every time. Always: as Auto from the first frame, also\nwhen the game makes its buffers again at another size.", "用于运行中会改变渲染分辨率的游戏。自动：一旦分辨率降到游戏的\n颜色缓冲以下，就用一个按所见最大分辨率构建的网络处理每一帧，\n画面在其中移动；此时网络的耗时等同于那个最大分辨率。\n精确：每个分辨率都重建网络，每次会有一两秒没有 NR。\n始终：从第一帧起就按“自动”的方式处理，游戏以其他尺寸\n重新创建缓冲时也一样。" },
{ "For inputs that use the 1080 tier: runs it on 1088 rows instead of 1152, about 4% faster.\nSlightly lossy, most at the bottom of the picture. Changing it rebuilds the model.\nThe new model always runs NVIDIA's 1152 rows.", "针对使用 1080 档的输入：用 1088 行而不是 1152 行来运行，约快 4%。\n略有损失，画面底部最明显。更改它会重建模型。\n新模型始终运行 NVIDIA 的 1152 行。" },
